  "author": "Dr. Lurie",
  "deck": "Sealing your face under an ointment overnight is an old dermatology trick with a new name. It is genuinely useful for one kind of skin and genuinely counterproductive for another.",
  "description": "What slugging is, the barrier science behind occlusion, the order the steps go in, who should skip it, and what to drop first if your skin objects.",
  "editorial": {
    "framework": "fw_routine",
    "writer_notes": "TOP-of-funnel routine guide. Chosen over fw_concern because the reader wants a sequence, and dry winter skin is common enough that a general routine is responsible. Dials under ceiling: claim_strength ~0.13, urgency 0, agitation ~0.03, cta_density ~0.05. One ask: the two-page occlusive card PDF, rendered from a purpose-built chromium template that crops and tones the hero in CSS and draws the layer diagram server-side."
  },
  "image": {
    "alt": "An open jar of plain clear ointment on a bedside table beside a folded flannel in low lamplight",
    "src": "/img/req_plugin_slugging_20260907_01/abef746fab351fa8b8f3eed073f2778fbfc10f706548db166cca75cbc3461820.webp"
